        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <description>Checks whether this Asset State Period belongs to the Asset and starts on or after the action&apos;s start date. A renewal or amendment starts a new period on that date, so it and any later periods get the new Number of Users; earlier periods keep theirs.</description>
        <name>Period_Matches_Action</name>
        <label>Period Starts On or After Action?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Loop_State_Periods</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Period_Matches</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Loop_State_Periods.AssetId</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <elementReference>Loop_Asset_Actions.AssetId</elementReference>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Loop_State_Periods.StartDate</leftValueReference>
                <operator>GreaterThanOrEqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <elementReference>Loop_Match_Sources.StartDate</elementReference>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Add_Period_Users</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Matches</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Runs when Revenue Cloud publishes the final Create Asset Order Event for an Order, meaning its Assets have been created after Order activation. First sets Number of Users on each of the Order&apos;s Assets from its Order Product (Order Product, then Asset Action Source, then Asset Action, then Asset), which creates the Beacon Subscriptions. It also records the users history: Number of Users and Change in Users on each Asset Action, and Number of Users on the Asset State Periods from the action&apos;s start date onward (0 users for a cancellation, which leaves the Asset unchanged). Then checks Assets Created on the Order, which starts Order - Assets Created - Create Renewal. The renewal work isn&apos;t done here because platform event-triggered flows can&apos;t call subflows or flow actions. Only listens to the event; it doesn&apos;t change it, so other subscribers still receive it. Only runs when Run Flows is checked on the On/Off Switch custom setting.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <description>Number of Users after this action: the Order Product&apos;s Number of Users, or 0 for a cancellation.</description>
        <name>formNewUsers</name>
        <dataType>Number</dataType>
        <expression>IF(TEXT({!Loop_Asset_Actions.Type}) = &quot;Cancel&quot;, 0, {!Loop_Match_Order_Items.Number_of_Users__c})</expression>
        <scale>0</scale>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <description>Change in Users for this action: the new Number of Users minus the Asset&apos;s Number of Users before this Order (0 when the Asset is new).</description>
        <name>formUsersChange</name>
        <dataType>Number</dataType>
        <expression>{!formNewUsers} - BLANKVALUE({!varPreviousUsers}, 0)</expression>
        <scale>0</scale>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>Create Asset Order Event - Mark Order Assets Created {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Create Asset Order Event - Mark Order Assets Created</label>
